-- הסכם עוז לתמורה (14.8.2011), §47 תוספת מעונות: from 1.9.2011, in place
-- of the day-care supplement paid on the eve of the signing, a teaching
-- employee who is the mother of a child under five is paid the
-- reimbursement for keeping a child in day care that §11 of the framework
-- agreement of 12.1.2011 sets — 300 a month for one child, 200 for a
-- second, two children at most, updated every January by the December
-- CPI — for the periods she is entitled to salary from the employer; an
-- expense reimbursement, not salary; a right connected with parenthood; it
-- replaces every other arrangement for a child under five, save a general
-- arrangement that pays more on both counts; subject to §29 of the Budget
-- Foundations Law.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT `oz-founding-common`
IMPORT `oz-founding-46`
IMPORT `oz-founding-conclusions`

§ `47 תוספת מעונות`

DECLARE `Oz section 47 action` IS ONE OF
    `decide the disagreement over a general day-care arrangement`

-- ¶1: from 1.9.2011 — the salary of September 2011, which (ז) names
-- (convention dates.salary-month) — in place of the "תוספת מעונות" paid on
-- the eve of the signing, the reimbursement of the expense of keeping a
-- child in day care that §11 of the framework collective agreement of
-- 12.1.2011 sets ("תוספת מעונות") is paid, as the section goes on to set
-- out. The section restates §11's terms, so the encoding reads them here;
-- the framework agreement is in the corpus and not yet encoded.
@ref akn:art_47/p1
`the first salary month of section 47` MEANS `the Oz salary month` 2011 9

GIVEN `the salary month` IS A NUMBER @desc as `the Oz salary month` counts it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 47 pays the day-care supplement in` `the salary month` IF
    `the salary month` AT LEAST `the first salary month of section 47`

`why the framework agreement's section 11 is not imported` MEANS
    `not yet encoded` "סעיף 11 להסכם הקיבוצי (מסגרת) מיום 12.1.2011, החזר הוצאות בעד החזקת ילד במעון"

§§ `47(א)–(ב)`

-- (א): the supplement is paid for a partial share in the expense of keeping
-- a child in day care or in other supervision, "by the conditions of
-- entitlement below": the purpose explains the supplement and adds no
-- condition of its own (convention precedence.rationale), and (ב) says no
-- receipt is asked. ¶2: a "child" is one who has not yet turned five,
-- unless said otherwise expressly. (ב): it is paid to a teaching employee
-- who is the mother of a child.
@ref akn:art_47__para_a akn:art_47__para_a/p2 akn:art_47__para_b
`the age a child of section 47 has not yet reached` MEANS 5

GIVEN `the child's age in whole years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a child for section 47` `the child's age in whole years` IF
    `the child's age in whole years` LESS THAN `the age a child of section 47 has not yet reached`

`section 47 asks the mother for receipts` MEANS FALSE

-- (ו)(3) below makes the supplement a right connected with parenthood under
-- §4(ב) of the Equal Employment Opportunities Law, 1988, and applies §4(א)
-- of that law to it, which says when such a right of a mother is a
-- father's too: that law is outside the corpus, so a father's entitlement
-- is not computed here.
@ref akn:art_47__para_b
GIVEN `a teaching employee who is a mother` IS A BOOLEAN
      `children under section 47` IS A NUMBER @desc her children who have not yet turned five
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the day-care supplement as a mother` `a teaching employee who is a mother` `children under section 47` IF
    `a teaching employee who is a mother` AND `children under section 47` AT LEAST 1

§§ `47(ג)–(ד)`

-- (ג): 300 a month for one child or the first child; 200 a month for a
-- second child. (ד): it is paid at once for two children at most.
@ref akn:art_47__para_c akn:art_47__para_c__subpara_1 akn:art_47__para_c__subpara_2 akn:art_47__para_d
`the day-care supplement for one or a first child, as signed` MEANS 300
`the day-care supplement for a second child, as signed` MEANS 200
`the children section 47 pays for at once` MEANS 2

GIVEN `children under section 47` IS A NUMBER
      `for a first child` IS A NUMBER
      `for a second child` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the day-care supplement for` `children under section 47` `for a first child` `for a second child` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `children under section 47` AT LEAST `the children section 47 pays for at once` THEN `for a first child` PLUS `for a second child`
        IF `children under section 47` AT LEAST 1 THEN `for a first child`
        OTHERWISE 0

§§ `47(ה)`

-- (ה): from January 2012 the amounts are updated once a year, in the
-- January salary, by the rate of change between the new index and the
-- previous one: the CPI the Central Bureau of Statistics publishes; the new
-- index is December's of the year before the month of the update; the
-- previous one is December's of the year before the previous update's
-- month, and for the first update December 2010's. Each update applies to
-- the amount in force on its day (convention dates.update-in-force),
-- exactly (convention rounding.default): given the December indices in
-- order, from December 2010 to the December before the last January
-- update, the amount moves by each year's ratio in turn.
@ref akn:art_47__para_e akn:art_47__para_e/p2 akn:art_47__para_e/p3 akn:art_47__para_e/p4 akn:art_47__para_e/p5
`the first salary month of section 47(ה)'s updates` MEANS `the Oz salary month` 2012 1

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      `the December indices` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc the CPI for December of each year, from December 2010 to the December before the last January update, in order
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a day-care amount updated each January` amount `the December indices` IS
    CONSIDER `the December indices`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN amount
    WHEN previous FOLLOWED BY later THEN
        CONSIDER later
        WHEN EMPTY THEN amount
        WHEN new FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `a day-care amount updated each January` (amount TIMES new DIVIDED BY previous) later

§§ `47(ו)`

-- (ו)(1): the supplement is paid only for a period for which the teaching
-- employee is entitled to salary from the employer and funded by it — not,
-- for instance, for a period of maternity pay under the National Insurance
-- Law, nor for unpaid leave. The rule asks it of the period.
@ref akn:art_47__para_f akn:art_47__para_f__subpara_1
GIVEN `entitled to salary from the employer, funded by it, for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 47 pays for the period` `entitled to salary from the employer, funded by it, for the period` IF
    `entitled to salary from the employer, funded by it, for the period`

-- (ו)(2): the supplement is a component of expense reimbursement and so not
-- salary for any purpose; contributions are made on it as is customary for
-- expense reimbursements — which, from 1.9.2011, §46(ג) says are the
-- agreement of 17.12.98's, at its rates.
@ref akn:art_47__para_f__subpara_2
`the day-care supplement is salary` MEANS FALSE

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `pension contributions on an Oz component`
DECIDE `the contributions on the day-care supplement on` d IS
    `the pension contributions section 46 makes on` d `an expense reimbursement`

-- (ו)(3): the supplement is a "right connected with parenthood" under
-- §4(ב) of the Equal Employment Opportunities Law, 1988, as amended from
-- time to time, and §4(א) of that law applies to it.
@ref akn:art_47__para_f__subpara_3
`why the Equal Employment Opportunities Law is not here` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "חוק שוויון ההזדמנויות בעבודה, התשמ\"ח-1988, סעיף 4"

§§ `47(ז)–(ח)`

-- (ז): from the salary of September 2011 the supplement replaces and
-- cancels every other arrangement on a child under five, whatever it is
-- called — a direct reimbursement or another benefit, directly or not, a
-- subsidy or a discount on day care among them.
-- (ח): notwithstanding (ז), it does not apply where there is a general
-- arrangement (of the employer, the workplace or the area) in which all of
-- these hold: (1) another benefit for a share in the cost of day care is
-- paid under it; (2) the benefit is above 300 a month for one child and
-- above 500 a month for two or more ("עולה על": convention
-- thresholds.above; the two together, as the text says). Then the general
-- arrangement goes on, by its own rules and with its standing unchanged,
-- "ובלבד שלא יחולו הסדרים כפולים": the mother has it and not the
-- supplement beside it. Whether the conditions hold is judged of the
-- arrangement, not of the teacher.
@ref akn:art_47__para_g akn:art_47__para_h akn:art_47__para_h__subpara_1 akn:art_47__para_h__subpara_2 akn:art_47__para_h/p2
`what a general arrangement must pay above for one child` MEANS 300
`what a general arrangement must pay above for two children or more` MEANS 500

GIVEN `it pays another benefit for day care` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its benefit for one or a first child` IS A NUMBER @desc a month
      `its benefit for two children or more` IS A NUMBER @desc a month
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a general arrangement section 47(ח) keeps` `it pays another benefit for day care` `its benefit for one or a first child` `its benefit for two children or more` IF
        `it pays another benefit for day care`
    AND `its benefit for one or a first child` `is above` `what a general arrangement must pay above for one child`
    AND `its benefit for two children or more` `is above` `what a general arrangement must pay above for two children or more`

DECLARE `what section 47 leaves a mother for day care` IS ONE OF
    `the day-care supplement of section 47`
    `the general arrangement section 47(ח) keeps`

GIVEN `under a general arrangement section 47(ח) keeps` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `what section 47 leaves a mother for day care`
DECIDE `what a mother is paid for day care under section 47` `under a general arrangement section 47(ח) keeps` IS
    IF `under a general arrangement section 47(ח) keeps`
    THEN `the general arrangement section 47(ח) keeps`
    ELSE `the day-care supplement of section 47`

-- (ח) ¶3: a disagreement over this goes to the steering committee (§59)
-- for decision (no deadline: convention dates.no-deadline).
@ref akn:art_47__para_h/p3
`deciding a disagreement over a general arrangement` MEANS
    PARTY `the steering committee`
    MUST  `decide the disagreement over a general day-care arrangement`

§§ `47(ט)`

-- (ט): for the avoidance of doubt, the section is subject to §29 of the
-- Budget Foundations Law, 1985. The agreement was approved under §29(א) on
-- the day it was signed (the sign-off, oz-founding-conclusions), so §29
-- lets it stand.
@ref akn:art_47__para_i
`section 29 lets section 47 stand` MEANS `section 29 lets the Oz agreement's changes stand`

§§ `47 -- the supplement of a month`

-- (א)–(ו) and (ח) together: the supplement for a salary month, from the
-- amounts as the December indices since December 2010 have updated them;
-- NOTHING before September 2011, when the eve's rules paid it.
GIVEN `the salary month` IS A NUMBER
      `a teaching employee who is a mother` IS A BOOLEAN
      `children under section 47` IS A NUMBER
      `entitled to salary from the employer, funded by it, for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under a general arrangement section 47(ח) keeps` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the December indices` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the day-care supplement under section 47 for the month` `the salary month` `a teaching employee who is a mother` `children under section 47` `entitled to salary from the employer, funded by it, for the period` `under a general arrangement section 47(ח) keeps` `the December indices` IS
    IF NOT `section 47 pays the day-care supplement in` `the salary month`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF     `entitled to the day-care supplement as a mother` `a teaching employee who is a mother` `children under section 47`
            AND `section 47 pays for the period` `entitled to salary from the employer, funded by it, for the period`
            AND `what a mother is paid for day care under section 47` `under a general arrangement section 47(ח) keeps` EQUALS `the day-care supplement of section 47`
         THEN JUST (`the day-care supplement for` `children under section 47`
                       (`a day-care amount updated each January` `the day-care supplement for one or a first child, as signed` `the December indices`)
                       (`a day-care amount updated each January` `the day-care supplement for a second child, as signed` `the December indices`))
         ELSE JUST 0

§§ `47 -- illustrations`

`no January update yet` MEANS EMPTY

#ASSERT `the day-care supplement under section 47 for the month` (`the Oz salary month` 2011 9) TRUE 1 TRUE FALSE `no January update yet` EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `the day-care supplement under section 47 for the month` (`the Oz salary month` 2011 9) TRUE 2 TRUE FALSE `no January update yet` EQUALS JUST 500
-- a third child adds nothing
#ASSERT `the day-care supplement under section 47 for the month` (`the Oz salary month` 2011 9) TRUE 3 TRUE FALSE `no January update yet` EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `the day-care supplement under section 47 for the month` (`the Oz salary month` 2011 8) TRUE 1 TRUE FALSE `no January update yet` EQUALS NOTHING
-- on maternity pay, or under a general arrangement (ח) keeps: none
#ASSERT `the day-care supplement under section 47 for the month` (`the Oz salary month` 2011 10) TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE `no January update yet` EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `the day-care supplement under section 47 for the month` (`the Oz salary month` 2011 10) TRUE 1 TRUE TRUE `no January update yet` EQUALS JUST 0
-- January 2012: December 2011's index 2% above December 2010's
#ASSERT `the day-care supplement under section 47 for the month` (`the Oz salary month` 2012 1) TRUE 2 TRUE FALSE (LIST 100, 102) EQUALS JUST 510
#ASSERT `a child for section 47` 4 AND NOT `a child for section 47` 5
#ASSERT `a general arrangement section 47(ח) keeps` TRUE 350 550
#ASSERT NOT `a general arrangement section 47(ח) keeps` TRUE 350 500
#ASSERT NOT `a general arrangement section 47(ח) keeps` TRUE 300 600
#ASSERT `the contributions on the day-care supplement on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2011) EQUALS JUST `under the agreement of 17.12.98, at its rates`
#ASSERT `section 29 lets section 47 stand`
